{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00342",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.66,
      "end_seconds": 5.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "I mean, hi there, is it alright if I come in now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.5,
      "end_seconds": 10.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Of course, put it down anywhere. So, how can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.85,
      "end_seconds": 27.24,
      "duration_seconds": 16.39,
      "text": "Okay, um, so I've been feeling a bit dizzy after taking all my tablets, and I wanted to get it checked. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.71,
      "end_seconds": 30.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "How long has this been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.39,
      "end_seconds": 33.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "About... well, about three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.74,
      "end_seconds": 37.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "How bad is it, would you say?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.97,
      "end_seconds": 45.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.94,
      "text": "I'd say mild. Right, I've been feeling confused about which tablets to take too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.65,
      "end_seconds": 50.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Is it all right if a trainee sits in later? No? Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.5,
      "end_seconds": 57.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "I, I'd rather not, if you don't mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.72,
      "end_seconds": 60.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Any fainting or falls?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.62,
      "end_seconds": 67.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "No, um, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.17,
      "end_seconds": 70.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Has there been any low mood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.03,
      "end_seconds": 72.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "No, no low mood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.71,
      "end_seconds": 77.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.92,
      "end_seconds": 81.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 81.94,
      "end_seconds": 90.26,
      "duration_seconds": 8.32,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Oxygen saturation is 97 percent, heart rate 77. Temp 36.7 degrees, BP is 128 over 73."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.7,
      "end_seconds": 92.4,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.53,
      "end_seconds": 96.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "One moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.53,
      "end_seconds": 97.35,
      "duration_seconds": 0.82,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.42,
      "end_seconds": 112.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Alright, any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.86,
      "end_seconds": 115.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Yes, I'm allergic to aspirin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.29,
      "end_seconds": 118.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Are you comfortable? Do you want some water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.42,
      "end_seconds": 123.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Yes, some water would be nice, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.1,
      "end_seconds": 127.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.22,
      "end_seconds": 136.52,
      "duration_seconds": 8.3,
      "text": "I've had arthritis in my knees for two years now. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.61,
      "end_seconds": 138.31,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Mm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.89,
      "end_seconds": 148.47,
      "duration_seconds": 8.58,
      "text": "Um, I have high blood pressure. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.23,
      "end_seconds": 173.3,
      "duration_seconds": 22.07,
      "text": "Okay. Right, so that's your known arthritis in my knees. We'll keep that in mind today. I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.23,
      "end_seconds": 176.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.19,
      "end_seconds": 177.89,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.65,
      "end_seconds": 180.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "I've never smoked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.73,
      "end_seconds": 185.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "Is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.04,
      "end_seconds": 197.4,
      "duration_seconds": 11.36,
      "text": "Yes, um, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.38,
      "end_seconds": 203.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Let's go through your medication. What are you taking? I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.93,
      "end_seconds": 211.19,
      "duration_seconds": 7.26,
      "text": "Paracetamol. I take it 650 milligrams, when needed. I'm on telmisartan, 40 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.09,
      "end_seconds": 215.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Let me just pull up your file for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.01,
      "end_seconds": 216.71,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.74,
      "end_seconds": 229.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.15,
      "end_seconds": 233.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Can I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.37,
      "end_seconds": 236.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Open wide for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.95,
      "end_seconds": 252.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Your blood pressure falls a little when you stand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.46,
      "end_seconds": 270.78,
      "duration_seconds": 14.32,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. I like to make sure you understand what's happening, so please stop me at any point. There are no silly questions, and I'd much rather you ask now than go home still wondering about something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.17,
      "end_seconds": 273.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Right, I understand now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.86,
      "end_seconds": 296.66,
      "duration_seconds": 19.8,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: It fits best with possible side effects from too many medicines. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've been feeling a bit dizzy after taking all your tablets for about three months, mild, and no fainting or falls."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 297.57,
      "end_seconds": 300.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "I mean, exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.24,
      "end_seconds": 305.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 306.36,
      "end_seconds": 321.41,
      "duration_seconds": 15.05,
      "text": "For the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.71,
      "end_seconds": 325.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange blood tests for medication review."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.2,
      "end_seconds": 329.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Sure, where do I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.67,
      "end_seconds": 352.33,
      "duration_seconds": 21.66,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an ECG for dizziness. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. Bring every box and bottle you have at home to the next visit, even the herbal ones, and we'll sort them together. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.73,
      "end_seconds": 360.29,
      "duration_seconds": 6.56,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if the symptoms get worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 360.84,
      "end_seconds": 364.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Hmm, you know, got it, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 366.12,
      "end_seconds": 374.74,
      "duration_seconds": 8.62,
      "text": "Please come and see me in a week. Just so I know I've explained it clearly, can you tell me the plan back in your own words?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 375.99,
      "end_seconds": 381.9,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "So, um, I come back in a week. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 383.13,
      "end_seconds": 387.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Wonderful, I think that's it. Ask me anything before you go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 388.51,
      "end_seconds": 392.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "That's everything I wanted to ask. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 393.01,
      "end_seconds": 393.76,
      "duration_seconds": 0.75,
      "text": "Take care."
    }
  ]
}